      "date": "January 2026",
      "summary": "Presents a high-conviction value thesis contending that Wall Street's focus on legacy branded checkout market share loss ignores PayPal's pivot toward high-margin digital plumbing and transaction data monetization. Outlines unit economics for Venmo debit card omnichannel integration, offsite targeted advertising across 438 million accounts, and potential banking license margin gains. Argues that growing TPV per active account combined with aggressive share repurchases makes stock re-rating mathematically inevitable.",
